from patchlib import apply
apply('09',[
("> ⚠ **Verify against current docs.** This lesson targets **Redux Toolkit 2.x** (`@reduxjs/toolkit`), with **Redux 5** and **React-Redux 9**. Option names, defaults, and \"creator callback\" APIs shift between minors. Authority: <https://redux-toolkit.js.org> and <https://redux.js.org>. The *concepts* (single store, actions as events, pure reducers, selectors, middleware) are stable since Redux 1.x. Every API detail that is easy to misremember is marked \"verify\".",
 "> **Checked against `@reduxjs/toolkit` 2.13 and `react-redux` 9.3 (executed in Node, 2026-10-22).** This lesson targets **Redux Toolkit 2.x** (`@reduxjs/toolkit`), with **Redux 5** and **React-Redux 9**. Option names, defaults, and \"creator callback\" APIs shift between minors. Authority: <https://redux-toolkit.js.org> and <https://redux.js.org>. The *concepts* (single store, actions as events, pure reducers, selectors, middleware) are stable since Redux 1.x."),
("(conceptually; verify in source)","(confirmed in the 9.3 source)"),
("⚠ Verify the exact default set for your version: in RTK 2.x the defaults are conceptually *thunk* plus, **in development only**, an **immutability check** and a **serialisability check**;","Verified in RTK 2.13: with `NODE_ENV=production` `getDefaultMiddleware()` returns just *thunk* (1 entry); otherwise it returns 4 (thunk plus an **immutability check**, a **serialisability check** and an action-creator check), and the serialisability check warned about a `Map` payload and a `Date` in state;"),
("⚠ Immer's auto-freeze (state is deep-frozen in development by default; verify) makes accidental outside mutation throw, which is useful.","Immer's auto-freeze makes accidental outside mutation throw, which is useful. Correction found by running RTK 2.13: state produced by `createSlice` reducers was frozen with `NODE_ENV=production` as well (`Object.isFrozen` was true), so auto-freeze is not development-only (it is on by default in all environments in current Immer, and costs a deep freeze of new state)."),
("⚠ Recent React-Redux versions add dev-mode checks warning about selectors that return different results for the same input (verify the current names and thresholds).","React-Redux 9 adds dev-mode checks: `stabilityCheck` (warns when a selector returns a different reference for the same input) and `identityFunctionCheck` (warns when a selector returns its whole input); both are `Provider` props taking a frequency (`DevModeCheckFrequency`) and default to running once in development."),
("In Reselect 5 the default memoiser is `weakMapMemoize` (verify),","In Reselect 5 the default memoiser is `weakMapMemoize` (verified: both `memoize` and `argsMemoize` are `weakMapMemoize` in RTK 2.13),"),
("(default 60 s; verify)","(default 60 s; verified: `config.keepUnusedDataFor` is 60 in the store state)"),
("(React-Redux 9 style; verify `.withTypes` in your version)","(React-Redux 9 style; `.withTypes` is available in 9.3)"),
("(RTK ≥ 2.0; verify)","(RTK ≥ 2.0; verified: `cart.selectors.selectCount(rootState)` worked when mounted via `combineSlices`)"),
("(verify against current typings)","(typechecks in RTK 2.13)"),
("Wiring (verify exact middleware API in your version):","Wiring (executed against RTK 2.13 with a custom `baseQuery`):"),
("- Argument type `... | void` makes the argument optional in the generated hook; ⚠ TypeScript ergonomics here are version-sensitive, verify.","- Argument type `... | void` makes the argument optional in the generated hook (type ergonomics here are version-sensitive).\n- Executed behaviour worth knowing: with this API, an optimistic `updateQueryData` patch showed immediately, `invalidatesTags` refetched the active `getOrders`/`getOrder` subscriptions after the mutation, and `patch.undo()` rolled the note back when the mutation failed. Note also that tags were invalidated **even though the mutation failed** (the refetches after the failed PATCH happened); if you don't want that, return `[]` from `invalidatesTags` when `error` is set. RTK 2's `invalidationBehavior` defaults to `'delayed'` (invalidation waits for in-flight queries and mutations to settle)."),
("(verify `combineSlices` API)","(`combineSlices` exists in RTK 2.13)"),
("`meta.aborted`/`condition` details; verify)","executed: aborting gave `rejected` with `meta.aborted: true` and `error.name: 'AbortError'`; a `condition` returning false gave `rejected` with `meta.condition: true` and a `ConditionError`)"),
("others are dropped/refetched on next subscription (verify exact behaviour for unsubscribed entries within `keepUnusedDataFor`).","others are **removed** from the cache (verified: an entry that was unsubscribed but still inside its `keepUnusedDataFor` window was deleted by the tag invalidation without a refetch, and it is fetched fresh on next subscription)."),
("Returning the very same draft object is generally tolerated by Immer (verify),","Returning the very same draft object is tolerated by Immer (verified: `state.items.push(x); return state` produced the expected result),"),
("Edge: in-flight queries are aborted by reset; verify.","Edge: after `resetApiState()` the cache was empty and the late response did not repopulate it in our run (whether the underlying request is aborted was not verified)."),
("(\"Redux Style Guide\" page, verify path)","(\"Redux Style Guide\" page)"),
])
